{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises","id":798447,"title":"Oaths made on false premises","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T16:04:22-08:00","id":798447,"title":"Oaths made on false premises","content":"I'm wondering what sort of interest story quirks could be derived from situations like this:<br /> &quot;But you swore an oath on your name that you'd get me through this safely&quot;<br /> &quot;The oath was 'I'll get you through this safely or my name isn't Jeremy Smith'. My name <b>isn't</b> Jeremy Smith. It's George Finch&quot;<br /> <br /> Though perhaps the issue would be whether or not the Wyrd would even be willing to sanctify such an oath and/or if it would fit the setting to have some way (probably Goblin Contract) to falsify the sensation of the Wyrd sanctifying an oath. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, thoughts on how the Wyrd would punish this kind of smart ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T16:58:11-08:00","id":798478,"title":"","content":"In the case of the example, the problem is that there's nothing for the Wyrd to anchor onto. The Wyrd is a connective force, but it can't connect a name to an action if there's no name to act on.<br /> <br /> Now, if you had a name not your own, literally owned it, it might work. But you'd have to be careful with <i>how</i> you owned it, less it become you, and the Wyrd snips you in the rear for breaking your promise.<br /> <br /> I could see a really cool Goblin Contract around that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:02:43-08:00","id":798520,"title":"","content":"There may not be a connection between the name and the action, but there's one between the two people, which is the oath. The oath binds them together, and if it is predicated on false basis, I'd say the Wyrd might be inclined to lapse upon other aspects of the character, such as other things the character expects people to do for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:16:29-08:00","id":798530,"title":"","content":"The staging on that is all wonky. If they tried it, it'd probably just end up as a Vow.<br /> <br /> You need to convince the Wyrd as your witness that you're [this person], and then dramatically reveal the actor beneath the role, [that person].<br /> <br /> But hell, whatever's more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T19:11:12-08:00","id":798552,"title":"","content":"I doubt it would work. An oath based on a condition that doesn't exist would simply fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T12:31:25-08:00","id":799740,"title":"","content":"P<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises?p=798530#post798530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The staging on that is all wonky. If they tried it, it'd probably just end up as a Vow.<br /> <br /> You need to convince the Wyrd as your witness that you're [this person], and then dramatically reveal the actor beneath the role, [that person].<br /> <br /> But hell, whatever's more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe talespinning with a disguise. After all it is a rather classic trope","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:28:49-08:00","id":800800,"title":"","content":"Oaths (with a capital O) need something strong to anchor onto, otherwise it can't support that sort of magical power. Names have power, thus you can use them for Oaths. Fake names that you invent on the fly... that's not as likely to work.<br /> <br /> However, maybe if you put extreme effort into establishing a fake name, used it for years as your fake identity and it had real meaning then it could support an Oath (in other words you spend XP on the Fake Identity merit). A Fake Identity with that sort of weight behind it, would probably be perceived by the Wyrd as similar to a Gentry's Title. However breaking that Oath would then have real consequences. Personally I'd say the Wyrd would slap you upside the head any time you were using that fake identity from then on but leave you alone the rest of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T07:14:09-08:00","id":801368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises#post798447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering what sort of interest story quirks could be derived from situations like this:<br /> &quot;But you swore an oath on your name that you'd get me through this safely&quot;<br /> &quot;The oath was 'I'll get you through this safely or my name isn't Jeremy Smith'. My name <b>isn't</b> Jeremy Smith. It's George Finch&quot;<br /> <br /> Though perhaps the issue would be whether or not the Wyrd would even be willing to sanctify such an oath and/or if it would fit the setting to have some way (probably Goblin Contract) to falsify the sensation of the Wyrd sanctifying an oath.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, thoughts on how the Wyrd would punish this kind of smart ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is clearly a smartly worded Vow with an easy loop hole, that is cleverly disguised as an Oath on a True Name, This is a staple of changeling and fae trickery, and why you never accept someone swearing on their True Name unless you are really sure you know it. There is even an example of people not accepting a real Oath on a person's True Name in <i>Changeling: the Lost</i> because they don't believe that's his actual True Name. That example wouldn't exist if it wasn't possible to pull this type of shenanigans. I'll post the page number when I get home tonight and have access to my books, unless someone posts a reply with the page number first.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd would totally sanctify this Vow, the fact that it appear to be an Oath and has a huge loop hole is immaterial. This is one reason why changelings are paranoid about wordings of Oaths and Vows. The Wyrd allows huge loop holes.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd specifically doesn't punish this type &quot;smart ass&quot; which is exactly why the True Fae are such horrible monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-05-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T08:17:48-08:00","id":801399,"title":"","content":"I think it's up to the Storyteller. Just like this is a classical trope, there's an equally classical trope about how the person that uses loopholes to dodge oaths and vows eventually gets punished by Fate. It's even written in many Fate spells in Mage, Fate does not like to be abused and taken for granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T09:56:34-08:00","id":801468,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, it seems like your example Oath there, &quot;I'll get you through this or my name isn't Jeremy Smith,&quot; (or something similar) could be a fun way to either get rid of or change your true name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T10:52:38-08:00","id":801506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises?p=801399#post801399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's up to the Storyteller. Just like this is a classical trope, there's an equally classical trope about how the person that uses loopholes to dodge oaths and vows eventually gets punished by Fate. It's even written in many Fate spells in Mage, Fate does not like to be abused and taken for granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is also true, and would love to see some type of comeuppance stat. I have Homebrew universally applicable version of Atrocity and Personal Banes for supernatural creatures in my games. It ties in well with the Death Clause and other supernatural means to cheat death.<br /> <br /> The above example, of leading someone to their doom while deceiving them into thinking you promised to keep them safe, is definitely an Atrocity. (Personal banes in my rules are things that cap dice pools by morality stat while applicable, inflict <i>resistant</i> damage with additional <i>resistant </i>aggravated damage based on Permanent Atrocity, and preclude supernatural defenses/cheating death)<br /> <br /> Atrocity in my games is the line between monsters and supernatural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-05-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:43:41-08:00","id":801532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises?p=801506#post801506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is also true, and would love to see some type of comeuppance stat. I have Homebrew universally applicable version of Atrocity and Personal Banes for supernatural creatures in my games. It ties in well with the Death Clause and other supernatural means to cheat death.<br /> <br /> The above example, of leading someone to their doom while deceiving them into thinking you promised to keep them safe, is definitely an Atrocity. (Personal banes in my rules are things that cap dice pools by morality stat while applicable, inflict <i>resistant</i> damage with additional <i>resistant </i>aggravated damage based on Permanent Atrocity, and preclude supernatural defenses/cheating death)<br /> <br /> Atrocity in my games is the line between monsters and supernatural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have that written up somewhere? Because with the 2.0 rework of Morality and the diverse Morality-equivalents, I find that there's a void in my Chronicles when it comes to the supernatural repercussions of doing Very Bad Things (and, for that matter, Very Good Things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T12:19:49-08:00","id":801548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798447-oaths-made-on-false-premises?p=801532#post801532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have that written up somewhere? Because with the 2.0 rework of Morality and the diverse Morality-equivalents, I find that there's a void in my Chronicles when it comes to the supernatural repercussions of doing Very Bad Things (and, for that matter, Very Good Things).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have a write up. It is based (roughly, I've re-written completely because a simple copy-paste was messy and wasn't 2.0e friendly) of Anchor to Sanity, Personal Banes and Atrocity from <i>Danse Macabre</i>. I'll post it in a thread with my homebrew rules tonight and edit this post with a link when I am done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:43:45-08:00","id":802320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> find that there's a void in my Chronicles when it comes to the supernatural repercussions of doing Very Bad Things (and, for that matter, Very Good Things).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\"> Homebrew of Pale_Crusader - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Frailty Chronicles Disclaimer* The follow Material is re-written homebrew adapting rules from Danse Macabre, Mirrors, and Walking Shadows (http://forum.theonyxpath. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Linked, I am not yet done but will be continuing to get everything over, finished written, and properly formatted over then next couple days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:24:22-08:00","id":803412,"title":"","content":"This took a little thinking. I couldn't quite put my finger on it but then I started trying to craft the pledge from the point of view of someone not trying to be tricky. Lots of changeling use false names after all. What would it look like for Mr Notmyrealname made this pledge. That's when it became obvious. They're swearing a Corporal pledge of a Mortal Emblem. They're risking their identity as that person. New Identity merit---gone. Ability to use that name anymore---Fate makes sure you can't.<br /> <br /> Task: Endeavor Guide to Safety -3<br /> Boon: Combat oriented Blessing +2<br /> Sanctions: NONE<br /> Duration: Day+1<br /> <br /> If they betray the person they are supposed to protect the pledge still breaks but nothing bad actually happens because of it. Well, aside from the potential Clarity loss and the Wyrd forcibly divesting you of your assumed identity. But if they're amoral enough to do this in the first place, that's not likely going to deter them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:45:56-08:00","id":803738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrickyBoots</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're swearing a Corporal pledge of a Mortal Emblem. They're risking their identity as that person. New Identity merit---gone. Ability to use that name anymore---Fate makes sure you can't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^THIS is a <u>brilliant</u> way to follow the Wyrd interpretation the wording in this way &gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowknight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's an equally classical trope about how the person that uses loopholes to dodge oaths and vows eventually gets punished by Fate. It's even written in many Fate spells in Mage, Fate does not like to be abused and taken for granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that as Storytellers we get to play the Genie-in-the-bottle when interpreting wording, and that by the vagueness of language it is almost always possible to twist things, or not twist things so that we are in a position to act as an arbiter of ironic cosmic justice.<br /> <br /> (Bonus points for having the opportunity for using 'ironic' correctly)<br /> <br /> Also I like the mental picture of the villains face after he sent the guy in the example to his doom and he tries to use his common alias again and it flat out fails to his frustration and possible serious detriment/ own personal doom.<br /> <br /> I can see an example where the person uses their fake ID to convince a rube that is their True Name, and that fake id counts as a mortal emblem unbeknownst to the rake using the ploy. He common uses that fake Id for his mortal identity, and then his life based on that Identity unravels for much heart ache and Clarity breaking points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-08-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}